As a result if a machine has multiple nics Assume eth0 and eth1 and i want kube traffic to go via eth1 and not via eth0.The above code would always cause eth0 to be picked up.And this become public IP of kube.
And there is no way to specify that eth1 should be only nic to be used.And public IP of kubernetes should be of nic eth1.
If this is a valid bug I suggest we support changing code in master.go line 195.and maybe adding a new variable in config files to define on which nic kube traffic should be allowed

As part of migrating everything to an official v1 api, we should remove the earlier versions from the code base and documentation on kubernetes.io

As part of this, I'm going to remove all the v1beta1 and v1beta2 specific code and test cases. I'm also going to update the scripts to stop generating swagger specs for them.

